al Mass: 14**\n\n### Refactored Code Mass (after)\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst SWORD_BASE_VALUE = 100;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 1 && items[0].type === \"sword\") {\n    const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(SWORD_BASE_VALUE * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n    return SWORD_BASE_VALUE + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items) }] };\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n}\n```\n- Constants: 12\n- Bindings: 7\n- Invocations: 4 (Math.ceil, calculateQuotePremium, two +)\n- Conditionals: 2\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\n**Total Mass: 35**\n\n### Refactoring Applied\n- Extracted `calculateQuotePremium(items)` to separate quote-premium logic from scenario orchestration.\n- Replaced magic number `115` with named components: `SWORD_BASE_VALUE + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE`, where `firstInsurance = ceil(base * 0.1)`. This reveals the intent behind the test comment: *100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee*.\n- Renamed local `quote` → `step` to reflect that `processScenario` currently handles only the first step.\n\n### Rule Assessment\n- **Rule 1 — Tests Pass**: all 2 active tests still pass.\n- **Rule 2 — Reveals Intent**: improved. The premium formula is now explicit, and quote calculation is isolated.\n- **Rule 3 — No Duplication**: no duplication yet; extracted helper provides a single place for quote logic.\n- **Rule 4 — Fewest Elements**: added constants and one helper; balanced by the clarity gained for the upcoming item-type tests.\n\n### Mass Change\n**14 → 35 (+21)**  \nMass increased because structure was added to make the calculation explicit. Per Simple Design Rule 2, clarity takes priority over lower mass here.\n\