ppy path.\n- `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS`, `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE`, `PROCESSING_FEE`: descriptive constants\n\n## Current Code Mass\n\nFocusing on the two active functions and the lookup constants:\n\n**`calculateQuotePremium`:**\n- Constants: `1`, `undefined` → 2\n- Bindings: `items`, `basePremium`, `firstInsurance`, `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS`, `PROCESSING_FEE`, `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE`, `Math` → 7\n- Invocations: `Math.ceil(...)` → 2\n- Conditionals: 2 `if`s → 8\n- Assignments: 2 `const` → 12\n- **Subtotal: 31**\n\n**`processScenario`:**\n- Constants: `\"quote\"` → 1\n- Bindings: `scenario`, `step`, `PROCESSING_FEE`, `calculateQuotePremium` → 4\n- Invocations: `calculateQuotePremium(...)` → 2\n- Conditionals: 1 `if` → 4\n- Assignments: 1 `const` → 6\n- **Subtotal: 17**\n\n**Global constants / lookup table:** ~47 (mostly from 6 `const` assignments)\n\n**Total: ~95**\n\n## Refactoring Plan\n\nMain issue: **conceptual duplication** in `calculateQuotePremium` — both guard clauses `return PROCESSING_FEE;`. I will:\n1. Extract the premium formula into a named helper so the success path reads as one concept.\n2. Combine the two guard conditions into a single ternary lookup, eliminating the duplicated fallback return.\n\nThis improves clarity (Rule 2) and removes duplication (Rule 3) at a small mass cost."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.write:3","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","content":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type Result = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface Results {\n  results: Result[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM = 100;\nconst AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM = 80;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: SWORD_BASE_PREMIUM,\n  amulet: AMULET_BASE_PREMIUM,\n  staff: STAFF_BASE_PREMIUM,\n};\n\nfunction calculatePremiumWithInsuranceAndFee(basePremium: number): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const basePremium = items.length === 1 ? ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type] : undefined;\n\n  if (basePremium === undefined) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  return calculatePremiumWithInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items) }] };\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":261,"output":8781,"cacheRead":7936,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7719,"totalTokens":16978,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925421087,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-50210444-1ec6-4903-b3a7-18e186b70063","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.write:3","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","