d** `isComponentItem(item)` to make the component-check in `calculateQuotePremium` self-documenting (`items.every(isComponentItem)`).\n\n### Duplication (Rule 3)\n- **Extracted** `basePremiumForType(type)` to provide a single representation for the \"lookup base premium with fallback to 0\" knowledge.\n- **Extracted** `calculateStandardBasePremium(items)` to give a name to the non-component premium path, removing the inline reduce duplication and making the ternary in `calculateQuotePremium` read like a clear branch decision.\n\n### Fewest Elements (Rule 4)\n- No unnecessary abstractions were removed because the existing code was already minimal for the 8 passing tests.\n- The added helper functions each serve a clear naming or duplication-removal purpose.\n\n## Tests\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (41 tests | 33 skipped)\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  8 passed | 33 todo (41)\n```\n\nAll tests remain green.\n\n## Decision Rationale\n\nMass increased slightly (+17) because the refactor introduced helper functions and a constant to improve intent and remove duplicated lookup logic. Per the Absolute Priority Premise guidelines, **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps mass**: the code now communicates *why* component items receive block pricing and centralizes the base-premium lookup. The small mass increase is acceptable because it pays for clarity and eliminates conceptual duplication.\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added component block logic for 3 alike components\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added component block logic for 3 alike components\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784925684851},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to refactor the implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping all tests green. This is a refactoring task. I need to:\n1. Read the implementation and test files\n2. Evaluate naming first\n3. Calculate APP mass before and after\n4. Apply Simple Design Rules in priority order\n5. Keep tests passing\n6. Document decisions\n\nLet me start by reading the relevant files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Let me start by examining the code and tests."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking && pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":85,"output":306,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":85,"totalTokens":5959,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925684870,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6ae2b1ba-691b-4554-81e5-ca39d474e428","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type Result = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface Results {\n  results: Result[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nfunction calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium: number): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nfunction calculateComponentBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const types = [...new Set(items.map((item) => item.type))];\n  return types.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const basePremium = items.every((item) => ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === 25)\n    ? calculateComponentBasePremium(items)\n    : items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items) }] };\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925687151},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Quote: empty and single-item base premiums\n  it(\"should quote premium 5 G for an empty item list -- only the processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }] });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 115 G for a single plain sword -- 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 71 G for a single plain amulet -- 60 base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 93 G for a single plain staff -- 80 base + 8 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 49 G for a single plain potion -- 40 base + 4 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 33 G for a single rune -- 25 base + 2.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 33 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: component blocks\n  it(\"should quote premium 60 G for 2 runes -- 50 base + 5 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 71 G for 3 runes -- 60 block base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 115 G for 4 runes -- 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 198 G for 7 runes -- 175 base + 17.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 88 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- 75 base + 7.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 137 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- 120 base + 12 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n\n  // Quote: item-specific modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 165 G for a cursed steel sword enchantment 3 -- 100 + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 145 G for a highly enchanted steel sword enchantment 5 -- 100 + 30 high enchantment + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 195 G for a cursed steel sword enchantment 5 -- 100 + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 143 G for a highly enchanted steel sword enchantment 4 cursed -- 100 + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\");\n\n  // Quote: policy-wide modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- 100 base - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 95 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- 100 base + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up + 5 fee = 100 G\");\n\n  // Quote: integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 165 G for newcomer with a cursed sword -- 100 + 50 + 10 + 5\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote premium 160 G for long-standing customer's second contract -- 100 + 50 + 30 + 10 - 15 - 20 + 5\");\n\n  // Quote: modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item in a multi-item policy -- cursed sword + plain amulet = 231 G\");\n\n  // Claim: standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for regular steel sword enchantment 3 damage 500 -- full reimbursement minus 100 deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 100 G for rune damage 200 -- full reimbursement minus 100 deductible\");\n\n  // Claim: enchantment threshold vs dragon material\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 -- 50% rule wins, then deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 700 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 5 damage 800 -- dragon material full, then deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 -- 50% rule, then deductible\");\n\n  // Claim: multiple items and damages\n  it.todo(\"should track cap 4000 G for a policy covering two swords\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item when two swords are damaged\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim that damages more items of a type than the policy covers\");\n\n  // Claim: cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce a second claim payout when remaining cap is exhausted -- 1400 then 600\");\n\n  // Quote/claim integration: insurance sum and cap\n  it.todo(\"should compute cap 3200 G for a policy covering a sword and an amulet\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value -- cursed sword cap 2000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should base insurance sum on individual component values, not block discount -- sword + 3 runes = 1750 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round a 197.5 G premium up to 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round a 350.5 G payout down to 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should error on quote with unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim referencing item not part of the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim with unknown damage item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim with negative damage amount\");\n\n  // Multi-step scenarios\n  it.todo(\"should process a quote followed by a claim against that policy\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925687151},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (41 tests | 33 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  8 passed | 33 todo (41)\n   Start at  20:41:26\n   Duration  149ms (transform 25ms, setup 0ms, collect 24ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925687151},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests pass. Now let me analyze the code for refactoring.\n\nCurrent code:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nfunction calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium: number): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nfunction calculateComponentBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const types = [...new Set(items.map((item) => item.type))];\n  return types.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const basePremium = items.every((item) => ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === 25)\n    ? calculateComponentBasePremium(items)\n    : items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items) }] };\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n}\n```\n\nNaming evaluation:\n- `processScenario` - OK, processes a scenario\n- `calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee` - descriptive but long. Maybe `applyFirstInsuranceAndFee`? Or `calculateFinalPremium`? Actually it reveals intent but is verbose.\n- `calculateComponentBasePremium` - OK, calculates base premium for component items\n- `calculateQuotePremium` - OK\n\nIssue 1: The special case `items.every((item) => ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === 25)` is checking if all items are \"component\" items (value 25). This is a bit magic - it reveals intent poorly. We should extract this into a named function or constant.\n\nIssue 2: The logic for component block has duplication - filtering items by type happens twice in `calculateComponentBasePremium`.\n\nIssue 3: The fallback branch `items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0)` duplicates the base premium calculation logic with the component block.\n\nIssue 4: `processScenario` always returns a premium result even for claim steps, returning the processing fee. This is likely placeholder behavior.\n\nIssue 5: Component block discount currently applies to all items that are worth 25. But what about moonstone? It's also 25. We have a test for 2 runes + 1 moonstone later. The current logic would treat 2 runes + 1 moonstone as component items because all are 25 base, and then calculate blocks per type. That seems right. But the current component block logic only groups by type, so 2 runes would be 50, 1 moonstone would be 25 = 75 base. Good.\n\nWait, but the todos show more tests. The component logic for 3 runes + 3 moonstones should be 120 base (60 + 60). Current logic: types are rune and moonstone, each count 3, each gets 60 = 120. Good.\n\nBut what about 7 runes? Current logic: count 7, not equal to 3, so 7 * 25 = 175. Good.\n\nWhat about 4 runes? count 4, not equal to 3, so 4 * 25 = 100. Good.\n\nThe logic is correct for current and foreseeable tests.\n\nRefactoring ideas:\n1. Extract a helper `areAllComponentItems` to clarify intent.\n2. Simplify `calculateComponentBasePremium` to avoid filtering twice.\n3. Maybe rename `calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee` to something shorter like `applyFirstInsuranceAndFee`.\n\nBut we must be careful not to over-engineer. Let's focus on Rule 2 (reveal intent) and Rule 3 (no duplication).\n\nPotential refactoring:\n- Create a function `isComponentItem(item: Item): boolean` to check if an item is a component (base premium 25).\n- Use it in `calculateQuotePremium`.\n- Simplify `calculateComponentBasePremium` by using `isComponentItem` and counting via reduce or by grouping.\n\nActually, let's think about mass. Current mass calculation:\n\nFor the whole file, let's count relevant elements in the implementation.\n\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5; // constant 1\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1; // constant 1\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100, // constants 6\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nfunction calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium: number): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3; // constant 1\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60; // constant 1\n\nfunction calculateComponentBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const types = [...new Set(items.map((item) => item.type))]; // invocation: map, Set constructor, spread (3 invocations?), bindings: types, item, item\n  return types.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const basePremium = items.every((item) => ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === 25)\n    ? calculateComponentBasePremium(items)\n    : items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const step = scenario.steps[0];\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items) }] };\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n}\n```\n\nAPP mass calculation is a bit subjective for the whole file. But we can focus on functions and count.\n\nActually, we need to attempt at least one refactoring. The most valuable one is improving intent around the component check and reducing duplication.\n\nLet me think of a clean refactor:\n\n```typescript\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\n\nfunction isComponentItem(item: Item): boolean {\n  return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const allComponentItems = items.every(isComponentItem);\n  const basePremium = allComponentItems\n    ? calculateComponentBasePremium(items)\n    : calculateStandardBasePremium(items);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n\nfunction calculateStandardBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n}\n```\n\nHmm, but that's adding more functions. We need to balance Rule 2 and Rule 4.\n\nActually, maybe a simpler refactor is to extract the base premium calculation:\n\n```typescript\nfunction calculateBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.every(isComponentItem)) {\n    return calculateComponentBasePremium(items);\n  }\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n}\n```\n\nThen `calculateQuotePremium` becomes:\n\n```typescript\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const basePremium = calculateBasePremium(items);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee(basePremium);\n}\n```\n\nBut that adds an indirection. Maybe not worth it.\n\nLet me think about duplication in `calculateComponentBasePremium`:\n- It does `items.filter((item) => item.type === type)` for each type.\n- It also does `items.map((item) => item.type)` to get types.\n\nCould group items by type first:\n\n```typescript\nfunction calculateComponentBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const countsByType = items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\n  return Object.entries(countsByType).reduce((sum, [type, count]) => {\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n```\n\nThis avoids multiple filters and is clearer. But uses `Object.entries` and a mutable accumulator. Hmm.\n\nAlternative:\n\n```typescript\nfunction calculateComponentBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  return [...counts.entries()].reduce((sum, [type, count]) => {\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n```\n\nThis is clearer but has higher mass.\n\nMaybe the simplest refactor is:\n1. Extract `isComponentItem` for clarity.\n2. Maybe rename `calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee` to `calculateFinalPremium`.\n\nLet me do the `isComponentItem` extraction and use it. That improves intent without much mass change.\n\nAlso, I notice the name `calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee` is very long. Maybe `calculateFinalPremium` or `applyFirstInsuranceAndFee`. Since the function's purpose is to take a base premium and return the final premium including first insurance and fee, `calculateFinalPremium` is shorter and still clear.\n\nAnother naming issue: `calculateComponentBasePremium` - maybe it should be `calculateComponentBlockPremium` since it applies block discount.\n\nActually, the most important thing is to reduce duplication. The expression `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0` appears in two places. We should extract a helper:\n\n```typescript\nfunction basePremiumFor(item: Item): number {\n  return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n}\n```\n\nThen:\n- `isComponentItem(item)` becomes `basePremiumFor(item) === COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM`\n- Standard premium calculation uses `basePremiumFor(item)`\n- Component premium calculation uses `basePremiumFor(type)` but wait, `basePremiumFor` takes an Item, not a type string.\n\nWe can have:\n\n```typescript\nfunction basePremiumForType(type: string): number {\n  return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n}\n\nfunction isComponentItem(item: Item): boolean {\n  return basePremiumForType(item.type) === COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n}\n```\n\nThis is getting better.\n\nLet me design the refactored code:\n\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nfunction basePremiumForType(type: string): number {\n  return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n}\n\nfunction isComponentItem(item: Item): boolean {\n  return basePremiumForType(item.type) === COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n}\n\nfunction calculateFinalPremium(basePremium: number): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nfunction calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const types = [...new Set(items.map((item) => item.type))];\n  return types.reduce((sum, type) => {\n    const count = items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * basePremiumForType(type);\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateStandardBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForType(item.type), 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const basePremium = items.every(isComponentItem)\n    ? calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items)\n    : calculateStandardBasePremium(items);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n  return calculateFinalPremium(basePremium);\n}\n```\n\nWait, `calculateStandardBasePremium` is a new function that adds an element. Is it worth it? It encapsulates the standard premium calculation and removes the inline duplication. But it might be overkill for 8 tests. Rule 2 says clarity over mass. I think it improves clarity.\n\nActually, the current code already has a decent structure. Let me reconsider.\n\nThe biggest issue is the magic number `25` in `items.every((item) => ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === 25)`. Extracting this to a constant and function is a clear win.\n\nThe duplication of `(ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0)` and `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0` can be addressed with `basePremiumForType`.\n\nLet me make these changes and calculate mass before/after.\n\nActually, I should be careful with `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` - the name change from `calculateComponentBasePremium` to `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` better reveals it handles blocks. Good.\n\nLet me also think about `processScenario`. It handles claims by returning processing fee. That's placeholder. For now, it might be fine. We could rename or leave it.\n\nLet me proceed with:\n1. Extract `basePremiumForType(type: string)`\n2. Extract `isComponentItem(item: Item)`\n3. Rename `calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee` to `calculateFinalPremium`\n4. Rename `calculateComponentBasePremium` to `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium`\n5. Extract `calculateStandardBasePremium(items: Item[])`\n\nThen run tests. If green, calculate mass.\n\nLet me first calculate initial mass. I'll focus on the implementation functions.\n\nCurrent implementation mass (excluding type declarations which are necessary):\n\nConstants:\n- PROCESSING_FEE = 5: 1\n- FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1: 1\n- ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS object literals (6): 6\n- COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3: 1\n- COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60: 1\n- Literal 25 in every check: 1\nTotal constants: 11\n\nBindings (variables/parameters):\n- calculatePremiumWithFirstInsuranceAndFee: basePremium (1), firstInsurance (1) = 2\n- calculateComponentBasePremium: items (1), types (1), sum (1), type (1), count (1), typePremium (1), item (map), item (filter) - hmm, arrow params. Let's count arrow function params as bindings too. map: item (1), filter: item (1). reduce: sum (1), type (1). = 8\n- calculateQuotePremium: items (1), basePremium (1), item (every) = 3\n- processScenario: scenario (1), step (1) = 2\nTotal bindings: 15\n\nInvocations:\n- Math.ceil: 1\n- basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE: * is not an invocation, it's an operat