"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:101","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring Complete.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|------|---------|------------|----------|\n| `calculateFinalPremium` | Adds base premium, item modifiers, first insurance, policy modifiers and processing fee | \"Final\" is vague — it actually computes the **total** premium | **Rename to `calculateTotalPremium`** |\n| `calculatePolicyModifiers` | Applies policy-wide adjustments such as loyalty discount | Name fits; follow-up contract discount is expected to land here | **Keep** |\n| New helper `countItemsByType` | Builds a frequency map of item types | Clearly reveals the grouping intent | **Add** |\n\n## Current Code Mass (before)\n\n```\nConstants:    30  →  30\nBindings:     46  →  46\nInvocations:  18  →  36\nConditionals:  7  →  28\nLoops:         6  →  30\nAssignments:   0  →   0\nTotal Mass:  170\n```\n\n## Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Renamed `calculateFinalPremium` → `calculateTotalPremium`**  \n   Better reveals that the function assembles the complete premium total.\n\n2. **Extracted `countItemsByType`**  \n   Replaced the separate `new Set(...)` + `items.map(...)` + `items.filter(...)` passes in `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` with a single grouping reduce. This removes scattered grouping logic and makes the block-pricing intent explicit.\n\n3. **Added explaining variable `unitPremium`**  \n   In `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium`, `basePremiumForType(type)` is now stored in `unitPremium`, clarifying that it is the per-item price for the type.\n\n4. **Grouped related constants**  \n   Moved component-block constants and loyalty constants closer to the functions that use them.\n\n## Refactored Code Mass (after)\n\n```\nConstants:    32  →  32\nBindings:     47  →  47\nInvocations:  18  →  36\nConditionals:  7  →  28\nLoops:         5  →  25\nAssignments:   0  →   0\nTotal Mass:  168\n```\n\n**Mass change:** `170 → 168` (Δ `-2`)\n\nThe small drop comes from eliminating one iteration (`filter`/`map`/`Set` replaced by one grouping reduce), partially offset by the new helper and the explaining variable.\n\n## Simple Design Rules Check\n\n1. **Tests pass** — `pnpm test` green before and after.\n2. **Reveals intent** — `calculateTotalPremium` and `countItemsByType` make the code self-describing.\n3. **No duplication** — item-type grouping now has a single representation.\n4. **Fewest elements** — one helper added; no unused code remains.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\npnpm test\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (41 tests | 24 skipped)\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  17 passed | 24 todo (41)\n```\n\nAll 17 active tests stay green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added loyalty discount policy modifier\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added loyalty discount policy modifier\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784925953608},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We are a refactor subagent. We need to refactor src/claim-office.ts with tests in src/claim-office.spec.ts, keeping all tests green. Need to attempt at least one refactoring, evaluate naming first, apply Simple Design Rules in priority order, calculate APP mass before/after,