yModifiers`: 3\n- binding `firstInsurance`: 1\n- assignment `=`: 6\n- invocation `Math.ceil`: 1\n- invocation `*`: 1\n- invocation `+` (4 additions): 4\n- constant `PROCESSING_FEE`: This is a reference to constant, not a new constant. But it's a literal value? No, it's a binding reference. In the example they didn't count references. So 0.\nTotal: 3+1+6+1+1+4 = 16\n\n#### calculatePolicyModifiers\n```ts\nfunction calculatePolicyModifiers(\n  basePremium: number,\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number {\n  let modifiers = 0;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD) {\n    modifiers -= basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  }\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n    modifiers -= basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  }\n  return modifiers;\n}\n```\n- bindings `basePremium`, `customer`, `quoteIndex`: 3\n- binding `modifiers`: 1\n- assignment `= 0`: 6 + 1 (constant) = 7\n- conditional `if` (years >= threshold): 4\n- conditional `>=`: 4\n- assignment `-=`: 6\n- invocation `*`: 1\n- conditional `if` (quoteIndex > 0): 4\n- conditional `>`: 4\n- assignment `-=`: 6\n- invocation `*`: 1\nTotal: 3+1+7+4+4+6+1+4+4+6+1 = 41\n\n#### calculateQuotePremium\n```ts\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number {\n  const basePremium = items.every(isComponentItem)\n    ? calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items)\n    : calculateStandardBasePremium(items);\n\n  if (basePremium === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const itemModifiers = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + calculateItemModifier(item), 0);\n  const policyModifiers = calculatePolicyModifiers(basePremium, customer, quoteIndex);\n  return calculateTotalPremium(basePremium, itemModifiers, policyModifiers);\n}\n```\n- bindings `items`, `customer`, `quoteIndex`: 3\n- binding `basePremium`: 1\n- assignment `= ... ? ... : ...`: 6\n- invocation `items.every`: 1\n- binding reference `isComponentItem`: 0\n- conditional `?:`: 4\