"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":228,"output":208,"cacheRead":72256,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":72692,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926155320,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d2ae8398-03e3-4f86-8ad1-ec2d8cd023a4","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:118","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete. All 22 passing tests still pass.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2)\n- `calculateItemSurcharges` → `calculateItemSurcharge`  \n  The function operates on a single `Item`, so the singular name accurately reveals intent.\n\n### Intent / Clarity (Rule 2)\n- Extracted magic number `10` in `calculateInsuranceSum` into `INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER`.  \n  The value `10` represented \"insurance value is 10× base premium\"; the named constant makes that relationship explicit.\n\n### Fewest Elements (Rule 4)\n- Removed unused `previousClaims` parameter from `calculateClaimResult`.\n- Removed unused `claims` array from `processScenario`.\n- Replaced the separate `quoteCount` counter and `quoteCount += 1` assignment with `const quoteIndex = policies.length`, which directly expresses \"the current quote's index equals the number of quotes already recorded.\"\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\nFocused on the changed regions (`calculateInsuranceSum`, `calculateClaimResult`, `processScenario`, and related constants).\n\n**Before refactor:**\n| Component   | Count | Mass |\n|-------------|-------|------|\n| Constants   | 7     | 7    |\n| Bindings    | 19    | 19   |\n| Invocations | 26    | 52   |\n| Conditionals| 2     | 8    |\n| Loops       | 3     | 15   |\n| Assignments | 2     | 12   |\n| **Total**   |       | **113** |\n\n**After refactor:**\n| Component   | Count | Mass |\n|-------------|-------|------|\n| Constants   | 6     | 6    |\n| Bindings    | 17    | 17   |\n| Invoc