lear\n- `findPolicyItem` - clear\n\nPotential naming issues:\n- `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE` - \"first insurance\" is a bit unclear. Maybe `NEW_POLICY_FEE_RATE` or `BASE_INSURANCE_FEE_RATE`? Looking at tests, they call it \"first insurance\". Hmm.\n- `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS` - fine\n- `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM` - fine\n- `calculateDamageReimbursement` - currently it handles high enchantment threshold by returning 50%, dragon material returns full. But the name is okay.\n- `DEDUCTIBLE` - fine\n- `INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER` - fine\n\n**Step 2: Calculate Initial APP Mass**\n\nI need to count components in the implementation file. Let me count carefully.\n\nConstants: PROCESSING_FEE, FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE, ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS (object literal count?), COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM, COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE, COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM, LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE, DEDUCTIBLE, INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE, DRAGON_MATERIAL.\n\nFor the object literal ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS, I need to decide how to count. Each key-value pair has literals. But let's count top-level constants as 1 each. The object entries inside are additional constants.\n\nActually, the instructions are not super precise. Let me count in a reasonable way:\n- Each literal value: 1\n- Each variable/parameter binding: 1\n- Each function call: 2\n- Each conditional: 4\n- Each loop: 5\n- Each assignment: 6\n\nLet me list the code and count.\n\nActually, I realize the APP mass calculation is somewhat ambiguous. Let me do my best to be consistent.\n\nFor `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = { sword: 100, ... }`:\n- Each value is a constant: sword=100, amulet=60, staff=80, potion=40, rune=25, moonstone=25 = 6 constants\n- The object assignment itself is an assignment = 6\n- Or maybe count the whole declaration as 1 binding? I'll count the