ion / hack** — Extracted generic `countBy<T>` helper. `countItemsByType` now delegates to it, and `validateClaim` uses `countBy` directly on damages instead of mapping damages into fake `Item` objects to reuse the helper. This removes conceptual duplication and reveals intent.\n\n3. **Unified parallel state** — Replaced parallel arrays `policies` and `remainingCaps` in `processScenario` with a single `policyStates: PolicyState[]` array. This removes a fragile parallel-array relationship and makes the connection between a policy and its remaining cap explicit.\n\n4. **Removed speculative guard** — In `calculateClaimResult`, after `validateClaim` guarantees every damaged item type exists in the policy, the `item !== undefined` ternary was unnecessary. Replaced it with a non-null assertion, removing a conditional branch that had no test coverage.\n\n## Step 7: Completion Report\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n- **Refactorings applied**: 4 (rename, extract `countBy`, unify policy state, remove speculative guard)\n- **Mass Change**: 294 → 283 (-11)\n- **Tests**: All green — 31 passed, 10 todo"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 31\nRecent Green phase: Tracked remaining cap per policy across claims\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 31\nRecent Green phase: Tracked remaining cap per policy across claims\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timesta