unt`:\n```ts\nreturn -(basePremium * (loyaltyRate + followUpRate));\n```\nInvocations: unary `-` (1), `*` (1), `+` (1) = 3\n\nAfter in `calculatePolicyDiscount`:\n```ts\nreturn basePremium * (loyaltyRate + followUpRate);\n```\nInvocations: `*` (1), `+` (1) = 2\n\nSo mass decreases by 1 (the unary minus).\n\nAnd in `calculateTotalPremium`:\nBefore:\n```ts\nreturn basePremium + itemModifiers + firstInsurance + policyModifiers + PROCESSING_FEE;\n```\nInvocations: `+` (4) = 4\n\nAfter:\n```ts\nreturn basePremium + itemModifiers + firstInsurance - policyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n```\nInvocations: `+` (3), `-` (1) = 4\n\nSame mass.\n\nSo total mass decreases by 1 from removing unary minus.\n\nThis is a nice improvement.\n\nBut wait, should I do both refactorings? The instructions say I MUST attempt at least one. I can do both. Let me do them sequentially.\n\nActually, I think I'll do:\n1. Remove redundant Math.floor in calculateClaimResult\n2. Rename and restructure the discount calculation\n\nLet me do them one at a time with test runs in between.\n\nLet me start with editing the file for the first change.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:4","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(totalPayout, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: Math.floor(remainingCap - payout) };","newText":"  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(totalPayout, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":255,"output":7516,"cacheRead":12160,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7417,"totalTokens":19931,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926611082,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-47140b26-b10c-471e-b12e-6b3b5357ddc9","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","t