\"cap is twice the insurance sum\" self-documenting\n\n### APP Mass Calculation — Base Premium Functions\n\n| Code | Mass |\n|------|------|\n| **Before** (`isComponentItem` + `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` + `calculateStandardBasePremium` + `calculateBasePremium`) | **61** |\n| **After** (`isComponentItem` + merged `calculateBasePremium`) | **48** |\n\n**Mass Change**: `61 → 48` (reduced by 13)\n\n### Simple Design Rules Check\n\n| Rule | Status |\n|------|--------|\n| 1. Tests Pass | ✅ All 37 tests passing, 4 todos unchanged |\n| 2. Reveals Intent | ✅ `calculatePolicyCap` names the cap rule; merged `calculateBasePremium` localizes base-premium logic |\n| 3. No Duplication | ✅ Removed two overlapping helper functions |\n| 4. Fewest Elements | ✅ Fewer functions and less indirection in base-premium path |\n\n### Tests\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (41 tests | 4 skipped)\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  37 passed | 4 todo (41)\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_20-33-25_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 37\nRecent Green phase: Added unknown item type validation for quotes\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 37\nRecent Green phase: Added unknown item type validation for quotes\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784926668606},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is invoking the refactoring subagent task. I need to refactor the implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping all tests green. I should evaluate naming first, apply Simple Design Rules, calculate APP mass before/after, and document decisions.\n\nLet me start by reading the implementation and test files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Let me start by reading the current files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":83,"output":119,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":62,"totalTokens":5770,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784926668627,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a9208a1d-84b8-4053-9657-8b200dd97f48","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type Result = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nexport interface Results {\n  results: Result[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nfunction basePremiumForType(type: string): number {\n  return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n}\n\nfunction isComponentItem(item: Item): boolean {\n  return basePremiumForType(item.type) === COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n}\n\nfunction countBy<T>(items: T[], keyFn: (item: T) => string): Record<string, number> {\n  return items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    const key = keyFn(item);\n    counts[key] = (counts[key] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n}\n\nfunction countItemsByType(items: Item[]): Record<string, number> {\n  return countBy(items, (item) => item.type);\n}\n\nfunction calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  const counts = countItemsByType(items);\n  return Object.entries(counts).reduce((sum, [type, count]) => {\n    const unitPremium = basePremiumForType(type);\n    const typePremium = count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n      ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n      : count * unitPremium;\n    return sum + typePremium;\n  }, 0);\n}\n\nfunction calculateStandardBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForType(item.type), 0);\n}\n\nfunction validateQuoteItems(items: Item[]): void {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] === undefined) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction calculateBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  validateQuoteItems(items);\n  return items.every(isComponentItem)\n    ? calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items)\n    : calculateStandardBasePremium(items);\n}\n\nfunction calculateItemSurcharge(item: Item): number {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForType(item.type);\n  const curseRate = item.cursed ? CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentRate = effectiveEnchantment(item) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return basePremium * (curseRate + enchantmentRate);\n}\n\nfunction calculateTotalPremium(\n  basePremium: number,\n  itemModifiers: number,\n  policyDiscount: number,\n): number {\n  const firstInsurance = Math.ceil(basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE);\n  return basePremium + itemModifiers + firstInsurance - policyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\nfunction calculatePolicyDiscount(\n  basePremium: number,\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number {\n  const loyaltyRate = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const followUpRate = quoteIndex > 0 ? FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  return basePremium * (loyaltyRate + followUpRate);\n}\n\nfunction calculateQuotePremium(\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number {\n  const basePremium = calculateBasePremium(items);\n  const itemModifiers = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + calculateItemSurcharge(item), 0);\n  const policyDiscount = calculatePolicyDiscount(basePremium, customer, quoteIndex);\n  return calculateTotalPremium(basePremium, itemModifiers, policyDiscount);\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER = 10;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nfunction effectiveEnchantment(item: Item): number {\n  return item.enchantment ?? 0;\n}\n\nfunction calculateInsuranceSum(items: Item[]): number {\n  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForType(item.type) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER, 0);\n}\n\nfunction findPolicyItem(items: Item[], itemType: string): Item | undefined {\n  return items.find((item) => item.type === itemType);\n}\n\nfunction calculateDamageReimbursement(damage: Damage, item: Item): number {\n  if (effectiveEnchantment(item) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    return damage.amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return damage.amount;\n}\n\nfunction validateClaim(claim: ClaimStep, policy: QuoteStep): void {\n  const damageCounts = countBy(claim.incident.damages, (damage) => damage.itemType);\n  const policyCounts = countItemsByType(policy.items);\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(damageCounts)) {\n    if (count > (policyCounts[type] ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(`Claim damages more ${type} items than policy covers`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction calculateClaimResult(\n  claim: ClaimStep,\n  policy: QuoteStep,\n  remainingCap: number,\n): ClaimResult {\n  validateClaim(claim, policy);\n  let totalPayout = 0;\n  for (const damage of claim.incident.damages) {\n    const item = findPolicyItem(policy.items, damage.itemType)!;\n    const reimbursement = calculateDamageReimbursement(damage, item);\n    totalPayout += Math.max(0, reimbursement - DEDUCTIBLE);\n  }\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(totalPayout, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n}\n\ninterface PolicyState {\n  policy: QuoteStep;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: Scenario): Results {\n  const policyStates: PolicyState[] = [];\n  const results: Result[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const quoteIndex = policyStates.length;\n      policyStates.push({\n        policy: step,\n        remainingCap: calculateInsuranceSum(step.items) * 2,\n      });\n      results.push({ premium: calculateQuotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer, quoteIndex) });\n    } else {\n      const state = policyStates[step.policy];\n      const result = calculateClaimResult(step, state.policy, state.remainingCap);\n      state.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926669552},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Quote: empty and single-item base premiums\n  it(\"should quote premium 5 G for an empty item list -- only the processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }] });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 115 G for a single plain sword -- 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 71 G for a single plain amulet -- 60 base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 93 G for a single plain staff -- 80 base + 8 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 49 G for a single plain potion -- 40 base + 4 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 33 G for a single rune -- 25 base + 2.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 33 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: component blocks\n  it(\"should quote premium 60 G for 2 runes -- 50 base + 5 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 71 G for 3 runes -- 60 block base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 115 G for 4 runes -- 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 198 G for 7 runes -- 175 base + 17.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 88 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- 75 base + 7.5 first insurance + 5 fee rounded up\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 137 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- 120 base + 12 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should quote premium 165 G for a cursed steel sword enchantment 3 -- 100 + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 145 G for a highly enchanted steel sword enchantment 5 -- 100 + 30 high enchantment + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 145 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 195 G for a cursed steel sword enchantment 5 -- 100 + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 195 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 115 G for a steel sword enchantment 4 -- no high enchantment surcharge, only first insurance and fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- 100 base - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on the second quote -- 100 base + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up + 5 fee = 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 100 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: integration examples\n  it(\"should quote premium 165 G for newcomer with a cursed sword -- 100 + 50 + 10 + 5\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it(\"should quote premium 160 G for long-standing customer's second contract -- 100 + 50 + 30 + 10 - 15 - 20 + 5\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 160 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote: modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item in a multi-item policy -- cursed sword + plain amulet = 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 231 });\n  });\n\n  // Claim: standard reimbursement\n  it(\"should pay out 400 G for regular steel sword enchantment 3 damage 500 -- full reimbursement minus 100 deductible\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n  });\n  it(\"should pay out 100 G for rune damage 200 -- full reimbursement minus 100 deductible\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"drop\", damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 });\n  });\n\n  // Claim: enchantment threshold vs dragon material\n  it(\"should pay out 400 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 -- 50% rule wins, then deductible\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n  });\n  it(\"should pay out 700 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 5 damage 800 -- dragon material full, then deductible\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 });\n  });\n  it(\"should pay out 400 G for steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 -- 50% rule, then deductible\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n  });\n\n  // Claim: multiple items and damages\n  it(\"should track cap 4000 G for a policy covering two swords\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 4000 });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item when two swords are damaged\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 },\n        ] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 600, remainingCap: 3400 });\n  });\n  it(\"should reject a claim that damages more items of a type than the policy covers\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 },\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 },\n        ] } },\n      ],\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  // Claim: cap exhaustion\n  it(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 3000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 2000, remainingCap: 0 });\n  });\n  it(\"should reduce a second claim payout when remaining cap is exhausted -- 1400 then 600\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] } },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 });\n    expect(result.results[2]).toEqual({ payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 });\n  });\n\n  // Quote/claim integration: insurance sum and cap\n  it(\"should compute cap 3200 G for a policy covering a sword and an amulet\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 3200 });\n  });\n  it(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value -- cursed sword cap 2000 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 2000 });\n  });\n  it(\"should base insurance sum on individual component values, not block discount -- sword + 3 runes = 1750 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 100 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 3500 });\n  });\n\n  // Rounding\n  it(\"should round a 197.5 G premium up to 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"should round a 350.5 G payout down to 350 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 350, remainingCap: 1650 });\n  });\n\n  // Error cases\n  it(\"should error on quote with unknown item type\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }],\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim referencing item not part of the policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim with unknown damage item type\");\n  it.todo(\"should error on claim with negative damage amount\");\n\n  // Multi-step scenarios\n  it.todo(\"should process a quote followed by a claim against that policy\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784926669552},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the implementation and tests. Let me run tests first to ensure they all pass, then perform the refactoring analysis.\n\nKey observations:\n1. The naming is generally good, but there are some areas to improve.\n2. There's conceptual duplication around \"component item\" identification and premium calculations.\n3. The `calculateBasePremium` function uses `items.every(isComponentItem)` which determines if all items are components. But the component block logic is a bit complex.\n4. `calculateInsuranceSum` uses `basePremiumForType(item.type)` but this function returns 0 for unknown types. However, for claims, the policy items should already be validated (quote validates them). So it's okay.\n5. The `calculateClaimResult` uses `findPolicyItem(policy.items, damage.itemType)!` with non-null assertion. This could be improved, but tests are passing and changing this might alter behavior.\n\nLet me think about refactorings:\n- Rename `isComponentItem` - it's checking if the base premium equals 25. The name is okay but \"component\" is domain term.\n- The `calculateBasePremium` function: it validates quote items, then checks if all items are components and uses component block pricing, otherwise standard. This is a bit odd because component block pricing is for when all items are components. But the component block premium function actually just uses `countItemsByType` and applies block pricing to ANY item type that has exactly 3. Wait, let me re-read.\n\n`calculateComponentBlockBasePremium`:\n- Count items by type\n- For each type, if count === 3 and unitPremium === 25, use 60; else use count * unitPremium\n\nSo if items include non-component items (sword, amulet, etc.), the function still handles them by `count * unitPremium`. But `calculateBasePremium` only calls it when `items.every(isComponentItem)`, so all items are components.\n\nThis is a bit of a code smell: `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` is general enough to handle non-component items, but `calculateBasePremium` restricts it. But actually, if we look at the test \"should base insurance sum on individual component values, not block discount -- sword + 3 runes = 1750 G\", the insurance sum uses `calculateInsuranceSum`, not `calculateBasePremium`. Insurance sum is always standard (count * unit premium * 10).\n\nSo the question is: can we simplify `calculateBasePremium`? Since `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` correctly handles both cases (when all components, and when mixed), why not always use it? Wait, but for non-component items with count 3, would it incorrectly apply block pricing? Let's check: sword has base premium 100, count 3 would give COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM=60 which is wrong. So we can't just always use it. We need the guard `items.every(isComponentItem)`.\n\nActually the current implementation is correct. Let me think about duplication:\n- `countBy` and `countItemsByType` - `countItemsByType` is just a specialization. This is okay.\n- `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` and `calculateStandardBasePremium` both iterate items.\n- `basePremiumForType` is used in multiple places.\n\nWhat about the non-null assertion in `calculateClaimResult`? The `validateClaim` function checks that the count of damages by item type doesn't exceed the count in policy. But it doesn't check that the damage item type exists at all in the policy. If `damage.itemType` is not in policy, `findPolicyItem` returns undefined and `!` will cause a runtime error. But there's an active test: `it(\"should reject a claim that damages more items of a type than the policy covers\")`. And there are todos for error cases. Since we must keep tests green and not break behavior, we shouldn't change this behavior yet. Actually, changing the undefined behavior might break the todo tests later if they expect specific error messages. But those are todos, so not active.\n\nLet me check the APP mass calculation for current code. I need to count components. But APP mass is typically done on the function being refactored. Let me focus on `processScenario` or maybe the whole file? The instructions say calculate APP mass before/after refactoring. I should pick a meaningful function or the whole file.\n\nLet me think of a concrete refactoring:\n\nRefactoring idea: Rename `firstInsuranceRate` to `FIRST_CONTRACT_RATE` or something more descriptive? Actually \"first insurance\" is domain terminology. Let me check tests - they call it \"first insurance\". So the name is appropriate.\n\nRefactoring idea: `calculateInsuranceSum` uses `basePremiumForType(item.type) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER`. We could extract a function `insuranceValueForItem` to clarify intent. But that adds elements.\n\nRefactoring idea: Simplify `calculateClaimResult` by extracting `deductibleReimbursement` or `payoutForDamage`. Actually the current code is clear enough.\n\nRefactoring idea: The `calculateTotalPremium` function parameters are `basePremium`, `itemModifiers`, `policyDiscount`. It computes first insurance and adds fees. This is fine.\n\nRefactoring idea: In `processScenario`, `policyStates` is mutated. Could we improve naming? `state` for the policy state is fine.\n\nRefactoring idea: The `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` function has nested logic that could be extracted. But it might add complexity.\n\nLet me look more carefully at duplication. `basePremiumForType(item.type)` appears many times. We could create a helper but it's already a helper.\n\nActually, a good refactoring target: `calculateStandardBasePremium` and `calculateInsuranceSum` are conceptually similar - both sum base premiums. The difference is only the multiplier. But applying DRY here might hurt clarity since one is base premium, the other is insurance sum.\n\nAnother target: `isComponentItem` checks if base premium equals `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM`. We could inline it but that hurts clarity.\n\nLet me consider a small but meaningful refactoring: Improve naming in `processScenario`. The variable `quoteIndex` is actually the policy index for the new quote. But `policyStates.length` gives the next index, so it's fine.\n\nI think a good refactoring is to extract the claim payout calculation logic to make it more readable, but that might not reduce mass.\n\nWait, I need to make at least one refactoring. Let me think about what would genuinely improve the code.\n\nLooking at `calculateBasePremium`:\n```typescript\nfunction calculateBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  validateQuoteItems(items);\n  return items.every(isComponentItem)\n    ? calculateComponentBlockBasePremium(items)\n    : calculateStandardBasePremium(items);\n}\n```\n\nThe `items.every(isComponentItem)` is doing two things: it's a guard for component block pricing. But it also means we validate items first. The validation is needed for both branches.\n\nCould we improve by making the function name of `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` more specific? It handles component blocks only when all items are components. Or we could move the `every` check inside that function. Let me think.\n\nActually, the block pricing rule is: \"if all items are components, apply block discount; otherwise standard\". The current split is reasonable.\n\nAnother idea: The `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` iterates all types, and for non-component types it would do `count * unitPremium` - but this branch is never reached because of the guard. We could assert or simplify. But it's defensive.\n\nLet me check for a real issue. In `calculateItemSurcharge`:\n```typescript\nfunction calculateItemSurcharge(item: Item): number {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForType(item.type);\n  const curseRate = item.cursed ? CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentRate = effectiveEnchantment(item) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return basePremium * (curseRate + enchantmentRate);\n}\n```\n\nThe variable `curseRate` and `enchantmentRate` are actually booleans-as-numbers. The intent could be clearer with `appliesCurseSurcharge` etc. But the current names are domain-aligned.\n\nWhat about extracting a function for `hasHighEnchantmentForQuote`? Not needed.\n\nLet me consider removing the `calculateStandardBasePremium` by making `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` correctly handle standard cases too. But as noted, it can't because of the block pricing risk.\n\nActually wait - we could refactor so that `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium` checks `isComponentItem` per type rather than relying on all items being components. Then we can always use it:\n\n```typescript\nfunction calculateBasePremiumForType(type: string, count: number): number {\n  const unitPremium = basePremiumForType(type);\n  return isComponentType(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * unitPremium;\n}\n```\n\nThen `calculateBasePremium` becomes:\n```typescript\nfunction calculateBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  validateQuoteItems(items);\n  const counts = countItemsByType(items);\n  return Object.entries(counts).reduce((sum, [type, count]) => sum + calculateBasePremiumForType(type, count), 0);\n}\n```\n\nThis would remove `isComponentItem`, `calculateComponentBlockBasePremium`, and `calculateStandardBasePremium`! That's a significant reduction. But wait, is it correct? The block pricing only applies when all items are components. With this per-type approach, if we have 3 swords, it would apply block pricing to swords, which is wrong per the current implementation.\n\nSo we need to keep the guard `items.every(isComponentItem)`. Unless the actual rule is \"component types get block pricing regardless\". But tests don't cover 3 swords. However, we can't change behavior not tested if it might break. Actually the current test suite doesn't test 3 swords. But the spec might intend that block pricing only applies to component-only quotes. Changing it could break future tests. So we should preserve the guard.\n\nAlternative: Keep the guard but merge the two functions:\n```typescript\nfunction calculateBasePremium(items: Item[]): number {\n  validateQuoteItems(items);\n  if (!items.every(isComponentItem)) {\n    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForType(item.type), 0);\n  }\n  const counts = countItemsByType(items);\n  return Object.entries(counts).reduce((sum, [type, count]) => {\n    return sum + (count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * basePremiumForType(type));\n  }, 0);\n}\n```\n\nThis removes the helper functions. But does it improve clarity? It might make the base premium calculation more localized.\n\nActually, I think a better r